item.description:
arXiv:2610.38168v1 Announce Type: new 
Abstract: In this article we investigate spherical maximal operators $\mathfrak m^\alpha$ of real order $\alpha$ acting on radial functions in the hyperbolic space $\mathbb H^n$. We show that for every $n\geq 2$, $1<p\leq\infty$ and $\alpha>(1-n)/2$, $\mathfrak m^\alpha$ is bounded on $L^p_{\mathrm{rad}}(\mathbb H^n)$ if and only if \begin{align*}
  \begin{cases}
  \alpha>1-n+\frac np, & 1<p\leq 2,
  \alpha>\frac1p-\frac{n-1}2, & 2<p\leq\frac{2n}{n-1},
  \alpha\geq\frac{1-n}p, & p>\frac{2n}{n-1}.
  \end{cases} \end{align*} Moreover, we show that for $1<p\leq 2n/(n-1)$ and \begin{align*}
  \alpha=
  \begin{cases}
  1-n+\frac np, & 1<p\leq 2,
  \frac1p-\frac{n-1}2, & 2<p\leq\frac{2n}{n-1},
  \end{cases} \end{align*} $\mathfrak m^\alpha$ is bounded from $L^{p,1}_{\mathrm{rad}}(\mathbb H^n)$ to $L^{p,\infty}_{\mathrm{rad}}(\mathbb H^n)$.
